config BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_CHECKPOINT
	bool "cadr-checkpoint"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_COMMON
	select BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_READOUT
	help
	  The checkpoint program. It reads the CADR's own memories
	  through the console's readout window and its main memory
	  through /dev/mem, and writes the whole machine as a muir
	  checkpoint. The file can then be opened in muir and resumed.

	  It digests the disk packs at the same instant and writes a
	  sidecar beside the checkpoint naming them, because a
	  checkpoint carries the blocks a run has written and never the
	  disk itself: resumed over a pack that has moved on, it
	  restores a machine into a disk it never had, and nothing in
	  muir can notice.

	  It halts the machine while it reads and starts it again
	  afterwards. It is not a daemon and has no init script: it is
	  run once, when somebody wants the machine in a file.
